# Build products.
#
# .build and .swiftpm are SwiftPM's; the rest are what Scripts/ assembles on the
# way to a release -- the app bundle, the archive it is submitted for
# notarization in, the help book it carries, and the disk image. All are
# reproducible from a clean checkout, and the disk image in particular is a
# signed artifact that belongs on a release page rather than in a repository.
.build/
.swiftpm/
DDCC.app/
DDCC.app.zip
DDCC.help/
DDCC.dmg

# docs/ is deliberately absent from this file. It is the generator's output, but
# Pages serves the site straight from it, so it is committed on purpose --
# `swift run SiteBuilder --check` is what keeps it honest against Sources/SiteGen
# and Site/.

# Signing and notarization material.
#
# signing.local.sh names this machine's keychain identity, so it differs per
# checkout by design. The rest are patterns rather than paths: an exported
# certificate or an App Store Connect key has no business in a public
# repository, and both arrive with default names from a download folder where
# it would be easy to drop one in the tree without noticing.
Scripts/signing.local.sh
*.p12
*.p8
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
*.provisionprofile

# Xcode's per-user state. SwiftPM needs none of it; opening the package in Xcode
# writes it anyway.
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/

# The font subsetter under Scripts/ is a maintainer tool that needs fonttools.
# Nothing in the build depends on it, so its interpreter's leavings and any
# environment created to run it stay out.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Written by Finder into any directory it is asked to display, including every
# directory of screenshot masters and site assets in this repository.
.DS_Store
